---
/**
 * /privacy — what the shop actually collects, grounded in the real order
 * flow (email only at checkout, no shipping address, no analytics, cart kept
 * in the browser's localStorage) rather than generic boilerplate. Still a
 * draft per the plan doc; have someone read it before launch.
 */
import LegalLayout from "@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What atk-collective.ch collects when you place an order, and why."
  heading="Privacy policy"
  updated="September 2026"
>
  <h2>Who this is</h2>
  <p>
    ATTAKK, Musterstrasse 1, 8000 Zürich, Switzerland (hello@atk-collective.ch)
    is responsible for the personal data described here, under the Swiss Federal
    Act on Data Protection.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>
    Browsing the shop and building a cart collects nothing — the cart lives only
    in your browser's local storage until you check out. Placing an order sends
    us your email address and the items and sizes you ordered — nothing else. We
    don't ask for a phone number or a shipping address, and we never see your
    card details, since payment is a bank transfer against a QR-bill rather than
    a card or a payment processor.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we use it</h2>
  <p>
    To confirm and fulfil your order, to email you the QR bill and pickup
    details, and to keep the accounting records Swiss law requires. We don't use
    your data for marketing. The one third party that sees it is our email
    provider (Infomaniak), which relays your confirmation and QR bill to your
    inbox; otherwise we don't share it with anyone outside ATTAKK.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
  <p>This site does not use tracking cookies or any third-party analytics.</p>

  <h2>Where it's stored</h2>
  <p>
    Order data is stored on our own server, not a third-party platform, and kept
    only as long as accounting and warranty obligations require.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us what we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to
    delete it once it's no longer needed for an order or for accounting, by
    writing to hello@atk-collective.ch.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
